implementationPlan.description:
Verification: ONE command. Its fresh output is the complete_task evidence, and QA re-runs it. It snapshots HEAD plus this task's three files under /mnt/d/moe-scratch, so peers' dirty bytes stay out. It then checks:
- under bash 3.2.57: the parse, plus the lease and git-guard suites (the guard suite launches the whole wrapper);
- that the skip is gone, and the ci.yml step's structure;
- under bash 5: the parse, parity-check, the four anchored node suites, and postflight-safe bash (DoD 4, about 20 min).
The architect ran this exact chain on the planned edits: VERIFY_EXIT=0, and postflight-safe printed {"engine":"bash","exit":0,"lastScenario":"Z","failureClass":"NONE"}.

Start it from the repo root with run_in_background, output redirected to a log. Wait with `until grep -q '^VERIFY_EXIT=' <log>; do sleep 10; done`, re-issued if it times out. Do not end the turn while it runs.

W=$(mktemp -d /mnt/d/moe-scratch/fa7fece5-XXXX) && git archive HEAD | tar -x -C "$W" && for f in scripts/moe-agent.sh scripts/tests/moe-account-lease.test.mjs .github/workflows/ci.yml; do cp "$f" "$W/$f"; done && cd "$W" && printf 'FROM node:24-alpine\nRUN apk add --no-cache python3 git ncurses-libs readline\nCOPY --from=bash:3.2 /usr/local/bin/bash /bin/bash\n' | docker build -q -t moe-bash32-probe:local - && docker run --rm -v "$W:/repo:ro" -w /repo moe-bash32-probe:local /bin/bash -c 'echo "bash $BASH_VERSION"; /bin/bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh && echo BASH32_PARSE_OK' && docker run --rm --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -e HOME=/tmp -v "$W:/repo:ro" -w /repo moe-bash32-probe:local node --test scripts/tests/moe-account-lease.test.mjs scripts/tests/agent-git-guard.test.mjs && ! grep -n -E 'bashVersion|before bash 4|known launcher bug' scripts/tests/moe-account-lease.test.mjs && python3 -c "import yaml; s=[x for x in yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/ci.yml'))['jobs']['build-all-platforms']['steps'] if '/bin/bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh' in x.get('run', '')]; assert len(s) == 1 and s[0].get('if') == 'runner.os == ' + chr(39) + 'macOS' + chr(39), s; print('CI_MACOS_PARSE_STEP_OK')" && bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh && bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && UNSET=$(env | grep -oE '^MOE_[A-Z_]+' | sed 's/^/-u /' | tr '\n' ' ') && env $UNSET node --test scripts/tests/moe-account-lease.test.mjs scripts/tests/agent-git-guard.test.mjs scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs scripts/tests/usage-launcher.test.mjs && env $UNSET node scripts/tests/postflight-safe.mjs bash; rc=$?; cd /mnt/d/projexts/moes; rm -rf "$W"; echo "VERIFY_EXIT=$rc"; [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]

Pass = VERIFY_EXIT=0, with:
- BASH32_PARSE_OK;
- the 3.2 suites at 0 fail (dry run: 64 pass, 1 Windows-only skip);
- CI_MACOS_PARSE_STEP_OK;
- PASS parity-check.sh;
- the bash 5 suites at 0 fail;
- postflight-safe failureClass NONE.

The completion summary must quote step 1's RED and GREEN probe output for /bin/bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh under 3.2.57 (DoD 1), and the 3.2 lease result (DoD 3). It must also state that macos-latest CI runs only on PRs to main. DoD 2's CI run and DoD 3's macOS-CI pass are therefore confirmed at the next CI PR. Until then, the local 3.2.57 run stands in; it reproduces the macOS error exactly. Never claim a CI run that did not happen.
